                     /label="rep pSC101"
                     /synonym="Replication protein"
                     /synonym="rep pSC101"
                     /note="rep pSC101 (RepA): the 316 aa replication initiation
                     protein that binds the pSC101 origin iterons and is
                     required in trans for replication. The allele here is the
                     one encoded by the pSC101 reference sequence NC_002056 (CDS
                     5273..6223, protein WP_010891056.1). It differs from
                     UniProt P22308 at two residues (P22308 reads H257 and Y289
                     where this one reads R257 and H289). Replication-deficient,
                     increased-copy-number and temperature-sensitive mutations
                     of pSC101 all map inside this gene, not in the origin
                     (Armstrong et al. 1984, which reports seven
                     replication-deficient insertions, four copy-number mutants
                     and one temperature-sensitive replication mutant within
                     rep101). That paper does not give the residue of the
                     temperature-sensitive allele, and no accessible source
                     checked here does, so this part claims no temperature
                     sensitivity for its own allele or for the two-residue
                     variant: the residue is unverified."
